%% Optional metering lifecycle, this is a mechanism view, not a second topology.
%%{init: {"sequence": {"useMaxWidth": true, "wrap": true, "diagramMarginX": 24, "diagramMarginY": 18, "actorMargin": 44, "messageMargin": 30}, "themeVariables": {"fontFamily": "Arial, sans-serif", "fontSize": "17px"}}}%%
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor User as Signed-in user
  participant OWUI as Open WebUI
  participant GW as AgentCore gateway + interceptor
  participant DB as DynamoDB ledger and pricing
  participant BR as Amazon Bedrock
  participant EV as EventBridge + debit
  participant OPS as Console + assurance jobs

  User->>OWUI: Send a model request
  OWUI->>GW: Cognito bearer access token + request payload
  GW->>DB: Read user USD policy, counter, RPM bucket, and rates

  alt Recorded spend is over limit or RPM is exhausted in ENFORCE mode
    GW-->>OWUI: OpenAI-shaped HTTP 429, next request is blocked
    OWUI-->>User: Present the upstream error through the active lane
  else Allowed, or OBSERVE mode
    GW->>DB: Write OPEN estimate and RPM tick
    GW->>BR: Invoke with gateway IAM role + project/workspace header
    BR-->>OWUI: Model response with provider usage when available
    OWUI->>EV: Seeded filter emits persisted normalized usage
    EV->>DB: Transactionally append ledger, add actual usage, subtract and close estimate
    DB-->>OPS: Serve self-service and admin usage views
  end

  par Daily or on-demand pricing and coverage
    OPS->>DB: Refresh AWS Price List rates and PRICING#_COVERAGE
  and Estimate recovery every five minutes
    OPS->>DB: Resolve OPEN estimates older than 15 minutes
    Note over OPS,DB: Refund is the default, settle-at-estimate is an operator configuration
  and Assurance signals
    OPS->>GW: Hourly block canary uses the real Chat Completions path
    OPS->>EV: Hourly capture canary begins at EventBridge
    OPS->>DB: Nightly D-2 token comparison uses account Cost Explorer data
  end

  Note over GW,DB: Availability first: unpriced calls remain available at $0 recorded cost, store and capture failures normally preserve chat, concurrent calls can cross a limit before the next-request block.
